\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Measured robustness and timing.} \textbf  {(a)} On the same 16 cells, the honest lagged-versus-lagged advantage is smaller than the asymmetric E2 estimate but remains ordered by $D_2$. The band is secondary and depends on the named corner set. \textbf  {(b)} In six R5 cells, retaining the calibration-time \emph  {policy choice} has p90 regret $1.00$ through 4,096 generated tokens, whereas freezing the token assignment costs $2.52$--$4.30\times $ a one-step-old assignment at the valid horizon.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:evidence}{{2}{4}{\textbf {Measured robustness and timing.} \textbf {(a)} On the same 16 cells, the honest lagged-versus-lagged advantage is smaller than the asymmetric E2 estimate but remains ordered by $D_2$. The band is secondary and depends on the named corner set. \textbf {(b)} In six R5 cells, retaining the calibration-time \emph {policy choice} has p90 regret $1.00$ through 4,096 generated tokens, whereas freezing the token assignment costs $2.52$--$4.30\times $ a one-step-old assignment at the valid horizon}{figure.2}{}}
